vel at home and a yellow envelope falls to the floor."},{"q":"Pourquoi Colette a-t-elle écrit cette lettre ?","q_en":"Why did Colette write this letter?","o":[{"fr":"Pour inviter Jeanne à manger des gâteaux","en":"To invite Jeanne to eat cakes"},{"fr":"Pour demander pardon à Jeanne","en":"To ask Jeanne for forgiveness"},{"fr":"Pour dire qu'elle quittait la ville","en":"To say she was leaving town"},{"fr":"Pour remercier Jeanne d'un cadeau","en":"To thank Jeanne for a present"}],"a":1,"why":"After a quarrel, Colette writes that she regrets it and ends with Pardonne-moi."},{"q":"Comment Hélène trouve-t-elle la famille de Jeanne ?","q_en":"How does Hélène find Jeanne's family?","o":[{"fr":"Elle trouve son numéro de téléphone","en":"She finds her phone number"},{"fr":"Le petit-fils de Jeanne vient à la librairie","en":"Jeanne's grandson comes to the bookshop"},{"fr":"Colette lui donne l'adresse","en":"Colette gives her the address"},{"fr":"Le libraire connaît la maison d'où vient le livre","en":"The bookseller knows the house the book came from"}],"a":3,"why":"The bookseller has no phone number but says the book came from a house on the rue des Tilleuls."},{"q":"Comment Hélène peut-elle appeler Colette ?","q_en":"How is Hélène able to call Colette?","o":[{"fr":"Un numéro est écrit au crayon sur l'enveloppe","en":"A number is written in pencil on the envelope"},{"fr":"Jeanne a gardé l'adresse de Colette","en":"Jeanne kept Colette's address"},{"fr":"Le jeune homme connaît son numéro","en":"The young man knows her number"},{"fr":"Le libraire lui donne le numéro","en":"The bookseller gives her the number"}],"a":0,"why":"Jeanne lost Colette's address, but Hélène sees a small number in pencil on the back of the envelope."},{"q":"Quelle est l'idée principale de l'histoire ?","q_en":"What is the main idea of the story?","o":[{"fr":"Il ne faut jamais lire les lettres des autres","en":"You should never read other people's letters"},{"fr":"Les vieux livres cachent toujours des secrets","en":"Old books always hide secrets"},{"fr":"On peut réparer une amitié, même très tard","en":"A friendship can be mended, even very late"},{"fr":"Les petites disputes n'ont pas d'importance","en":"Small quarrels do not matter"}],"a":2,"why":"After forty years Jeanne tells Colette it is never too late, and the two friends will meet again on their bench."}]}